\details{
A queue of object keys (\code{"namespace/name"}) with the semantics of
client-go's rate-limited work queue, which is what controllers use
between their informers and their reconcile function:
\itemize{
\item A key is queued at most once. Ten events for one object before it is
handled still mean one reconcile.
\item A key is never handed out twice at the same time. If it is added again
while being processed, it goes back on the queue when \code{done()} is
called, so the change is not lost.
\item \code{add_after()} makes a key available after a delay (for "check again in
a minute"). If a key is delayed twice, the earlier time wins.
\item \code{add_rate_limited()} re-adds a key after a per-key exponential backoff
(\code{base_delay}, doubling up to \code{max_delay}); \code{forget()} resets it after
a success.
}

The usual loop is \code{key <- q$get()}, reconcile, then \code{q$forget(key)} on
success or \code{q$add_rate_limited(key)} on failure, and finally
\code{q$done(key)}.
}
\examples{
q <- WorkQueue$new()
q$add("default/web"); q$add("default/web")
q$len()              # 1
key <- q$get()
q$add_rate_limited(key)   # failed: retry after base_delay
q$done(key)
q$next_ready_in()
}
